Q: Roughly how much PTO do I accrue each month?
   Flow: FOLLOWUP → FOLLOWUP → END
   Turns: 4, Tools: 0, Corrections: 0, Verifications: 0
   👤: Roughly how much PTO do I accrue each month?
   🤖: Based on our company policy, you receive 20 days of PTO per year, accrued monthly. This averages out to approximately **1.67 days** of PTO accrued each month (20 days divided by 12 months).
   👤 [FOLLOWUP]: That makes sense. How many of those PTO days are allowed to roll over to the next year?
   🤖: According to our policy, you are allowed to roll over up to **5 unused PTO days** to the next year.
   👤 [FOLLOWUP]: That's good to know. Do unused sick days also roll over to the next year?
   🤖: No, unused sick days do not roll over to the next year. You receive 10 sick days per year, and any unused days will expire at the end of the year.
   👤 [END]: That clears things up. Thank you for the information!

